WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.060
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level B one.

2
00:00:05.360 --> 00:00:08.677
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:08.977 --> 00:00:16.018
Unit fourteen: Modals of Obligation (must/have to). Today you will talk about rules, duties and things that are not necessary.

4
00:00:16.318 --> 00:00:18.982
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:19.933 --> 00:00:23.364
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:24.217 --> 00:00:25.055
Must.

7
00:00:26.050 --> 00:00:29.222
Must means a strong obligation, often from the speaker.

8
00:00:29.817 --> 00:00:31.816
I must finish this today.

9
00:00:32.417 --> 00:00:34.697
Your turn. Say: Must.

10
00:00:37.533 --> 00:00:38.337
Must.

11
00:00:39.083 --> 00:00:39.945
Have to.

12
00:00:40.950 --> 00:00:43.994
Have to means an obligation from a rule or situation.

13
00:00:44.583 --> 00:00:46.281
I have to wear a uniform.

14
00:00:46.883 --> 00:00:49.350
Your turn. Say: Have to.

15
00:00:52.200 --> 00:00:53.189
Have to.

16
00:00:53.950 --> 00:00:55.056
Don't have to.

17
00:00:56.050 --> 00:00:58.270
Don't have to means it is not necessary.

18
00:00:58.883 --> 00:01:00.140
You don't have to come.

19
00:01:00.750 --> 00:01:03.309
Your turn. Say: Don't have to.

20
00:01:06.167 --> 00:01:07.377
Don't have to.

21
00:01:08.117 --> 00:01:09.025
Mustn't.

22
00:01:10.017 --> 00:01:11.796
Mustn't means it is forbidden.

23
00:01:12.383 --> 00:01:14.116
You mustn't smoke here.

24
00:01:14.717 --> 00:01:17.079
Your turn. Say: Mustn't.

25
00:01:19.933 --> 00:01:20.818
Mustn't.

26
00:01:21.583 --> 00:01:22.759
Obligation.

27
00:01:23.750 --> 00:01:26.133
Obligation means something you must do.

28
00:01:26.717 --> 00:01:28.589
Homework is an obligation.

29
00:01:29.183 --> 00:01:31.894
Your turn. Say: Obligation.

30
00:01:34.733 --> 00:01:35.955
Obligation.

31
00:01:36.717 --> 00:01:37.706
Necessity.

32
00:01:38.717 --> 00:01:41.006
Necessity means something that is needed.

33
00:01:41.617 --> 00:01:43.593
Water is a necessity.

34
00:01:44.183 --> 00:01:47.126
Your turn. Say: Necessity.

35
00:01:49.967 --> 00:01:51.026
Necessity.

36
00:01:51.783 --> 00:01:52.483
Rule.

37
00:01:53.483 --> 00:01:55.518
Rule means an official instruction.

38
00:01:56.117 --> 00:01:57.106
Follow the rule.

39
00:01:57.717 --> 00:02:00.218
Your turn. Say: Rule.

40
00:02:03.067 --> 00:02:04.091
Rule.

41
00:02:04.850 --> 00:02:05.816
Prohibition.

42
00:02:06.817 --> 00:02:09.385
Prohibition means an order not to do something.

43
00:02:09.983 --> 00:02:11.646
There is a prohibition here.

44
00:02:12.250 --> 00:02:14.717
Your turn. Say: Prohibition.

45
00:02:17.567 --> 00:02:18.521
Prohibition.

46
00:02:19.333 --> 00:02:22.798
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:23.650 --> 00:02:26.184
Visal, tell me one rule at your school.

48
00:02:27.283 --> 00:02:38.448
We have to wear a uniform. Have to shows an obligation from a rule or situation. Must is often a personal feeling: I must call my mother.

49
00:02:39.550 --> 00:02:41.503
What is the difference in the negative?

50
00:02:42.617 --> 00:02:51.701
Don't have to means it is not necessary: You don't have to pay. Mustn't means it is forbidden: You mustn't use your phone in the exam.

51
00:02:52.817 --> 00:02:54.445
Is that a common mistake?

52
00:02:55.550 --> 00:03:04.788
Yes. Many learners say mustn't when they mean it is not necessary. Remember: don't have to is a choice, mustn't is a prohibition.

53
00:03:05.933 --> 00:03:07.410
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:08.250 --> 00:03:12.014
Grammar focus: Must, have to, don't have to, mustn't.

55
00:03:12.314 --> 00:03:13.594
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:14.283 --> 00:03:15.900
We have to wear a uniform.

57
00:03:16.783 --> 00:03:18.504
You don't have to pay today.

58
00:03:19.417 --> 00:03:21.660
You mustn't use a phone in the exam.

59
00:03:22.600 --> 00:03:29.971
Must / have to = obligation. Don't have to = not necessary. Mustn't = forbidden. They are not the same.

60
00:03:30.717 --> 00:03:35.218
Be careful! Don't say: You mustn't pay. It's free.

61
00:03:37.167 --> 00:03:40.040
Say: You don't have to pay. It's free.

62
00:03:40.340 --> 00:03:41.956
Mustn't means forbidden.

63
00:03:42.767 --> 00:03:45.582
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:46.367 --> 00:03:47.635
Rules and Duties.

65
00:03:47.935 --> 00:03:50.457
At my school, we have to wear a uniform.

66
00:03:51.467 --> 00:03:53.664
We must arrive before seven thirty.

67
00:03:54.667 --> 00:03:57.293
We don't have to wear shoes inside the classroom.

68
00:03:58.300 --> 00:04:00.659
We mustn't use phones during an exam.

69
00:04:01.667 --> 00:04:05.094
A rule is an obligation, and a prohibition is a strong rule.

70
00:04:06.200 --> 00:04:10.527
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:11.383 --> 00:04:14.117
You blank smoke here. It is forbidden.

72
00:04:14.417 --> 00:04:18.349
A, don't have to. B, mustn't. C, haven't to.

73
00:04:21.900 --> 00:04:23.737
The answer is B: mustn't.

74
00:04:24.883 --> 00:04:27.373
You blank come. It is optional.

75
00:04:27.673 --> 00:04:31.280
A, mustn't. B, don't have to. C, must.

76
00:04:34.833 --> 00:04:37.019
The answer is B: don't have to.

77
00:04:38.183 --> 00:04:40.206
I blank wear a uniform at school.

78
00:04:40.506 --> 00:04:44.241
A, have to. B, am have to. C, has to.

79
00:04:47.800 --> 00:04:50.113
The answer is A: have to.

80
00:04:51.250 --> 00:04:53.157
Which sentence means 'forbidden'?

81
00:04:53.457 --> 00:04:57.795
A, You don't have to enter.. B, You mustn't enter.. C, You can enter..

82
00:05:01.333 --> 00:05:03.867
The answer is B: You mustn't enter..

83
00:05:05.017 --> 00:05:07.655
According to the reading, what must students do?

84
00:05:07.955 --> 00:05:12.874
A, arrive before seven thirty. B, bring food. C, wear shoes inside.

85
00:05:16.433 --> 00:05:19.710
The answer is A: arrive before seven thirty.

86
00:05:20.900 --> 00:05:23.843
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:24.683 --> 00:05:27.774
Write one sentence with 'must' and one with 'don't have to'.

88
00:05:36.583 --> 00:05:38.165
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:05:38.465 --> 00:05:49.758
I must finish my homework before dinner. I don't have to wake up early on Sunday, so I can rest. I use must for obligation and don't have to when something is not necessary.

90
00:05:50.058 --> 00:05:51.790
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:05:52.683 --> 00:05:57.762
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and must, have to, don't have to, mustn't.

92
00:05:58.062 --> 00:06:02.282
Today's value is responsibility. Help at home and do your jobs.

93
00:06:02.582 --> 00:06:05.072
See you in Unit fifteen. Goodbye!

94
00:06:05.372 --> 00:06:08.187
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

